#%PAM-1.0
# PAM stack for the Auros kiosk session.
#
# This is NOT a login path. Nobody authenticates here: systemd starts the service as auroskiosk and
# uses PAMName purely so that systemd-logind registers a session, assigns seat0 and creates
# XDG_RUNTIME_DIR. Without a registered session the compositor has no seat and no runtime directory.
#
# auth is pam_permit because there is no credential to check -- the account has no password and is
# not reachable from outside. The account restrictions live in polkit, sudoers and the account's
# nologin shell, not here.
auth        required    pam_permit.so
account     required    pam_permit.so
session     required    pam_permit.so
session     optional    pam_keyinit.so force revoke
session     optional    pam_loginuid.so
session     optional    pam_systemd.so class=user type=wayland
